  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "R1 and R8 directly establish that hybrid Monte Carlo/atomistic simulation can generate and compare random and SRO states in a bcc refractory HEA, while R2, R3, R5, R6, R10, and R16 show that thermal treatment or simulation can tune local chemical order and ordered nanostructures in other multicomponent alloys. Separately, R4 and R7 connect chemical or force-constant disorder to phonon scattering and thermal transport, and R9 provides an example of nanoscale compositional pathways or layering in a refractory alloy. These strands suggest studying thermal transport as SRO is varied, but none discloses HfTi/TiZr cluster percolation, B2-like pathways, reduced lattice distortion, or the resulting conductivity increase in HfNbTaTiZr. Combining SRO control with a percolative heat-conduction mechanism therefore still requires a substantial new idea."
}
